   502	  /// [stream] Pick-and-compact consumer: removes the one-shot-read memory floor.
   503	  ///
   504	  /// MEASURED: `loadExperiment` reaches 90.3 GB RSS / 99.0 GB peak at t=0s, BEFORE any compaction
   505	  /// exists — so the compact store (10 B/peak, 20.9 GB for 2.19e9 peaks) can never lower the peak.
   506	  /// The floor is the whole run being resident at once. BrukerTimsFile::loadDIAStreaming hands us one
   507	  /// frame at a time, so we peak-pick and compact each frame on arrival and never hold the raw run.
   508	  ///
   509	  /// Windows are keyed by the SAME (lo,hi) isolation-window key used downstream, taken from the
   510	  /// spectrum's own precursor, so routing is identical to the old split - not by swath_nr, whose
   511	  /// ordering is the reader's business and need not match ours.
   512	  class PickCompactConsumer : public FullSwathFileConsumer
   513	  {
   514	  public:
   515	    PickCompactConsumer(PeakPickerIM& picker, map<pair<int, int>, vector<CompactFrame>>& windows,
   516	                        PeakMap& ms1, CompactStats& stats,
   517	                        std::function<pair<int, int>(double, double)> keyfn)
   518	      : picker_(picker), windows_(windows), ms1_(ms1), stats_(stats), keyfn_(std::move(keyfn)) {}
