  2683	    //-------------------------------------------------------------
  2684	    // [route-1] FEATURE-LEVEL CONSOLIDATION
  2685	    //
  2686	    // We emit 4.6 PSMs per unique peptide; diaTracer emits 1.46. We are not producing WORSE spectra
  2687	    // (purity 8.3% vs their 4.0%) - we are producing the SAME peptide many times while missing others.
  2688	    // Emission is per precursor HYPOTHESIS (per trace), not per chromatographic FEATURE, so one real
  2689	    // feature can be emitted from several RT slices / IM sub-ranges / charge hypotheses.
  2690	    //
  2691	    // Consolidate: spectra whose precursors agree in m/z (ppm), RT and IM are ONE feature -> keep the
  2692	    // single best (most fragments, then most intense) and drop the rest. This changes emission
